> roots of z^3 = 1
  ucas: it(z) = z^3 - 1
  ucas: zeros it
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
zeros of it (z complex):
  3 roots (a polynomial of degree 3):
    z = -1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2
    z = -1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2
    z = 1
  check: |it| <= 2e-16 at the roots; the polynomial's coefficients come from 64 samples and were checked at 8 other points
  a polynomial of degree 3 has 3 complex roots counted with multiplicity (the fundamental theorem of algebra)
