> zeros of x^2 = 4
  ucas: it(x) = x^2 - 4
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  2 zeros:
    x = -2
    x = 2
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
> roots of x^2 = x + 1
  ucas: it(x) = x^2 - (x + 1)
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  2 zeros:
    x = (1 - sqrt(5))/2
    x = (1 + sqrt(5))/2
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
> roots of x^2 = -x
  ucas: it(x) = x^2 - (-x)
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  2 zeros:
    x = -1
    x = 0
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
