> find the zeros of sin x = 1/2 on [0, 7]
  note: x taken as real on [0, 7] (say "integer x" for whole numbers)
  ucas: it(x: real in 0..7) = sin(x) - 1/2
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  3 zeros on [0, 7]:
    x = 0.5235987756 (~pi/6)
    x = 2.617993878 (~5*pi/6)
    x = 6.806784083 (~13*pi/6)
  checked numerically, grid of 20001 points: sign changes refined by bisection, touching zeros at critical points; zeros between grid points that do not change sign can be missed
> zeros of (x^2 = 4)
  ucas: it(x) = x^2 - 4
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  2 zeros:
    x = -2
    x = 2
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
> zeros of x & 7 = 3 for an unsigned 8-bit x
  ucas: it(x: u8) = (x & 7) - 3
  ucas: zeros it
zeros of it:
  32 zeros in 0..255: x = 3, 11, ..., 251 (every 8)
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points
> zeros x^2 = 4
  note: '=' inside an expression read as '=='
zeros of x^2 - 4:
  2 zeros:
    x = -2
    x = 2
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
> zeros (x: u8) & 7 == 3
  note: bitwise operators bind tighter than comparisons here (unlike C): read as ((x & 7) == 3)
zeros of (x & 7) - 3:
  32 zeros in 0..255: x = 3, 11, ..., 251 (every 8)
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points
