> zeros of x & 7 < 3 for an unsigned 8-bit x
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x & 7 < 3
  ucas: zeros it
  note: bitwise operators bind tighter than comparisons here (unlike C): read as ((x & 7) < 3)
zeros of it:
  160 zeros in 0..255: x = 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 27, ...
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points
> the period of x & 7 = 3 for an unsigned 8-bit x
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x & 7 == 3
  ucas: period it
  note: bitwise operators bind tighter than comparisons here (unlike C): read as ((x & 7) == 3)
period of it:
  fundamental period 8
  proved, exhaustive: f(x + 8) = f(x) for every x with both in 0..255, and no smaller shift works
  the pattern also continues across the wrap-around of the type (the period divides the domain size)
